**Foundational Stuff:**

* [MCMAS: an open-source model checker for the verification of multi-agent systems](https://d-nb.info/1125527056/34), Lomuscio et al 2015
* Halpern, Joseph Y, Reasoning about uncertainty, The MIT Press, 2003.
* [Reasoning About Knowledge](https://www.cs.rice.edu/~vardi/papers/book.pdf), Fagin et al 1995

**Languages, Engines, Tools, Resources for Model Checking**

* [wiki://model checking](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Model_checking)
* [wiki://Binary_decision_diagram](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Binary_decision_diagram)
* **Tools:**
	* [github://johnyf/tool_lists](https://github.com/johnyf/tool_lists/blob/main/verification_synthesis.md): index of tools for verification and games
	* [github://albertocasagrande/pymodelchecking](https://github.com/albertocasagrande/pyModelChecking)
	* [github://marcusm117/mctk](https://github.com/marcusm117/mctk): kripke structures / model checking logic from scratch in python 
	* [ELVis: Epistemic logic visualizer](https://nomuras.github.io/ELVis/)
	* [A cheatsheet/overview](https://mluckcuck.github.io/model-checking-cheatsheet) of the popular stuff, including SPIN, PRISM, etc.
	* [ghio://tyche](https://tychelibrary.github.io/), a library for aleatoric description logic
**Engines:**
	* [wiki://tla+](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TLA%2B)
	* [Prism model checker](https://www.prismmodelchecker.org/), uses PCTL
	* **mCRL2**
		* formal-spec toolset: [https://www.mcrl2.org/web/index.html](#) 
		*[mcrl2 algebra](https://www.mcrl2.org/web/user_manual/fundamentals/basic_modelling.html)
	* [gh://jrclogic/SMCDEL](https://github.com/jrclogic/SMCDEL) model checker with [PAL]({{mkdocs.site_relative_url}}/opref#PAL) support
	* [gh://sysulic/MEPK](https://github.com/sysulic/MEPK) A general multi-agent epistemic planner based on higher-order belief change
	* [gh://msakai/haskell-decision-diagrams](https://github.com/msakai/haskell-decision-diagrams) BDDs lib in haskell
* **Papers/Lectures/Etc:**
	* **MCK** 
		* Gammie, Peter, and Ron Van Der Meyden, ‘MCK: Model checking the logic of knowledge’, in Computer Aided Verification, Springer, 2004,
		* [MCK solver whitepaper](https://cgi.cse.unsw.edu.au/~meyden/research/mck-white-paper.pdf) (an alternative to MCMAS also supporting epistemic logic)
	* [Montanari lecture slides](https://users.dimi.uniud.it/~angelo.montanari/Intro-MC.pdf), with an intro to model checkers 
	* [SMV language lectures](https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~emc/15414-f11/lecture/lec13_SMV.pdf), mentioned as inspiration for ISPL. (2011)
	* [Scaling Multi-Agent Epistemic Planning through GNN-Derived Heuristics](https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.12840) (2025)
	* [A process algebraic framework for multi-agent dynamic epistemic systems](https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.17537) (2024)
	* [A Computationally Grounded, Weighted Doxastic Logic](https://chentaolue.github.io/pub-papers/sl16.pdf) Chen et al 2015
	* Intro to [PAL / Public Announcement Logic](https://builds.openlogicproject.org/content/applied-modal-logic/epistemic-logic/public-announcement-logic-lang.pdf)
	* [Kh logics](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2106.11504), i.e. Know-how vs Know-that. Wang, Li, 2021
	* Resources for [MCAPL](https://autonomy-and-verification.github.io/tools/mcapl) (model checking agent programming language) ~2023
	
